From: openrc2 ASan rollout (Hunt-Subagent, verifiziert im Gast)
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] execute_function: dispose copied body in pipe subshell

ASan-Bash meldet beim Beenden jeder Pipeline-Subshell Leaks und LSan
erzwingt Exit 1: execute_function() registriert uw_dispose_command() und
uw_maybe_restore_getopt_state() nur fuer subshell == 0. Der
Pipe-Subshell-Zweig hat keinen Unwind-Frame; kopierter Funktionsbody +
getopt-State verwaist. Folge: `f | filter`-Pipelines liefern PIPESTATUS 0=1,
was Portages __save_ebuild_env-Pipeline (alle Merge-Phasen) abbricht.
Unsanitisiert unsichtbar, identische Version verhaelt sich ohne ASan normal.

--- a/execute_cmd.c
+++ b/execute_cmd.c
@@ -5426,6 +5426,12 @@
 	pop_args ();
     }
 #endif
+  if (subshell)
+    {
+      /* The unwind protects above that dispose the copied function body and restore the getopt state are only registered when subshell is 0. A function run in a subshell, such as the left side of a pipeline, exits right after this; free those explicitly. Otherwise leak checkers report them at subshell exit and clobber the status the parent sees in PIPESTATUS. */
+      dispose_command (tc);
+      uw_maybe_restore_getopt_state (gs);
+    }
 
   function_misc_cleanup ();
   return (result);
